<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Rich Gang AI backup policy (SECURITY_REVIEW SEC-07, decided
  2026-10-23 in the flagship sweep):

  Preference data is DEVICE-LOCAL and is never backed up: the
  shared-preferences domain holds character mind state, Danny's
  ledger/self-upgrade state, the discernment record, per-character
  provider IDs, Stage overrides — and the age-assurance record.
  Age-assurance state in particular must never ride a backup into
  a "restored verification": excluding the whole domain is the
  fail-closed way to guarantee that.

  The daemon's SQLite store file (app files dir, wired in P6) is
  excluded for the same reason: its datasets are local state, and
  its future content is not backup-cleared.

  Provider API keys live in Keystore-backed secure storage and are
  not part of Auto Backup.

  A new or restored device therefore starts with fresh local
  state. That is the policy, stated here rather than inherited
  from platform defaults.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
    <exclude domain="file" path="rich_gang_ai/daemon_store.sqlite3" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="rich_gang_ai/daemon_store.sqlite3-wal" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="rich_gang_ai/daemon_store.sqlite3-shm" />
</full-backup-content>
